From 449d75e49e719fe3d59ff6f8b34c9dfd9d4bfad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:33:21 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a3xx: don't push UBOs into the fragment shader's
 const file

a306 hangs when the CP's indirect state DMA targets the fragment shader's
constant file.  The packet is

  CP_LOAD_STATE { DST_OFF = .. | STATE_SRC = SS_INDIRECT
                | STATE_BLOCK = SB_FRAG_SHADER | NUM_UNIT = .. }
               { STATE_TYPE = ST_CONSTANTS | EXT_SRC_ADDR = <ubo> }

which fd3_emit_const_bo() builds for every pushed UBO range whose backing
store is a buffer object, i.e. for the ranges that
ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges() lowers from UBO loads to constant-file reads.

If an earlier draw in the same submit has left a fragment context
resident, the draw that follows such an upload never starts.  The GPU
parks in the front end with

  RBBM_STATUS 0xe0684003   HI_BUSY | CP_ME_BUSY | CP_NRT_BUSY
                           | PC_DCALL_BUSY | VFD_BUSY | VPC_BUSY | HLSQ_BUSY
  CP_WFI_PEND_CTR 0x1, CP_STQ_AVAIL 16, CP_HW_FAULT 0

and SP_BUSY, TPL1_BUSY, RB_BUSY, TSE_BUSY, RAS_BUSY, UCHE_BUSY and
VBIF_BUSY all clear: no wave is ever dispatched, nothing faults, and the
CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE behind the upload never retires, so msm's hangcheck
fires with a completed/submitted fence gap of 3.

The minimal reproducer is two GPU operations in one batch: a scissored
glClear followed by a GSK rounded-clip gradient glDrawArraysInstanced.
Removing either operation, or splitting them across submits with
FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem,flush, avoids the hang; so does
IR3_SHADER_DEBUG=nouboopt.  Rebuilding that pair on a host under the
freedreno drm-shim with FD_GPU_ID=307 and diffing the command streams,
the only packet present in the hanging stream and absent from every
passing one is the SS_INDIRECT ST_CONSTANTS load into SB_FRAG_SHADER.
The vertex stage issues the same packet from the same buffer, at the same
DST_OFF and with the same NUM_UNIT, in every passing stream, so the
discriminator is the state block and not indirect const loads in general.

Two other readings were tried on the hardware and refuted.  Splitting the
upload into chunks of const_upload_unit (8 vec4, the largest const upload
in any stream this part has ever run clean) still hangs, so it is not the
transfer size; setting HLSQ_CONTROL_0_REG's CHUNKDISABLE,
LAZYUPDATEDISABLE or SINGLECONTEXT individually still hangs.  Emitting
the identical payload to the identical destination with STATE_SRC =
SS_DIRECT instead passes, which leaves the CP's indirect fetch into the
fragment block as the failing element.

So stop lowering UBO loads to the constant file for the fragment stage on
gen < 4 and let it use ldg, keeping every other stage - in practice the
vertex stage - exactly as before.  The cost is that a3xx fragment shaders
lose push constants entirely; that is the same trade
IR3_SHADER_DEBUG=nouboopt makes, and freedreno-a306-skips.txt has been
skipping spec@arb_uniform_buffer_object@rendering-array and
rendering-array-offset under a "# Hangchecks" heading for years.

Hardware validation: the identical code path was tested as a build-time
knob on a DragonBoard 410c (APQ8016, Adreno A306, revision 307, chip id
03000600) running Linux 7.3.0-0.rc3 aarch64 and Mesa 26.2.2.  Three clean
runs of the minimal pair against three hangs on the unmodified driver,
then the full apitrace under FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem, then the full apitrace
on the default GMEM path with no FD_MESA_DEBUG at all - all clean, with
matching retired/submitted fences, no devcoredump and no hangcheck.  This
patch as written has so far only been checked on the host to produce the
expected command stream.

Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/12634
Cc: mesa-stable
Signed-off-by: Sam Day <me@samcday.com>
---
 .../ir3/ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c          | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c
index 0c3570db..9cd7e33d 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges.c
@@ -654,6 +654,28 @@ ir3_nir_analyze_ubo_ranges(nir_shader *nir, struct ir3_shader_variant *v)
    if (ir3_shader_debug & IR3_DBG_NOUBOOPT)
       return;
 
+   /* a3xx cannot push UBO data into the fragment shader's constant file.
+    *
+    * A pushed range whose backing store is a buffer object is uploaded by
+    * the CP with a CP_LOAD_STATE { STATE_SRC = SS_INDIRECT } { ST_CONSTANTS }
+    * (see fd3_emit_const_bo()), i.e. the CP DMAs the data straight into the
+    * on-chip constant RAM.  On a306 that transfer wedges HLSQ whenever the
+    * state block is SB_FRAG_SHADER and a draw from earlier in the same
+    * submit has left a fragment context resident: the following draw parks
+    * in the front end with HLSQ_BUSY asserted, SP/TPL1/RB/UCHE all idle and
+    * no waves ever dispatched, and the CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE behind it never
+    * retires.  The same packet is fine for SB_VERT_SHADER from the same
+    * buffer at the same offset and size, and an inline (SS_DIRECT) upload of
+    * the identical payload into SB_FRAG_SHADER is fine too, so it is the
+    * indirect fetch into the fragment block specifically that is broken.
+    *
+    * Keep pushing for every other stage and let the fragment shader read its
+    * UBOs with ldg instead.  (This is what IR3_SHADER_DEBUG=nouboopt has been
+    * doing for the a306 UBO deqp job all along, but for both stages.)
+    */
+   if (compiler->gen < 4 && v->type == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT)
+      return;
+
    uint32_t upload_remaining = max_upload;
    bool push_ubos = compiler->options.push_ubo_with_preamble;
 
-- 
2.55.0

